{
  "comment": "Run authority and refusal codes of the caller proxy in shared application mode (ADR 0239 'Bundle, identity and request contract' items 2 and 3; the run and work_item pair and the deadline bound stand from ADR 0178). In shared mode the proxy (apps/worker/src/curie_connector_proxy/shared.py) verifies the X-Curie-Caller cct2 token with caller.decide_shared against its configured installation, then takes the invocation's run and work_item only from the verified token (shared.run_context): a tool in the application policy's run_tools refuses run_required when the token carries no pair, and inbound X-Curie-Run / X-Curie-Work-Item headers, tool arguments and the session never supply a pair. The handle's expires_at is the token's exp, which the worker already capped to the run deadline at mint. `cases` drive the pure decision (decide_shared then run_context at `now` for `installation`) and the real proxy, fixture MCP server and resolver socket, where expect.context is what the shared server's resolution reports. `deadline`, when not null, is the run deadline the token was minted under: expires_at never exceeds it and always equals claims.exp. `refusals` is the frozen shared refusal table: code, HTTP status and the curie_caller value (one of the five in tests/vectors/connector-caller-refusal.json, which is not extended); the body is the dedicated JSON-RPC refusal with error.data.curie_shared set to the code. body_encoding_unsupported refuses any request body carrying a Content-Encoding other than identity, which the proxy cannot inspect as JSON. Every token is stored as its \".\"-separated segments, exactly token.split(\".\"), signed by the seed of the first vector of tests/vectors/connector-caller-token.json (`signed_by` names it), so no whole token string appears here; readers join the segments with \".\". Read by apps/worker/tests/connector_proxy/test_shared_proxy_run_authority.py, which rejects an unknown key so a key added for one reader cannot pass vacuously, and by the shared proxy's refusal assertions in apps/worker/tests/connector_proxy/_shared_proxy_harness.py.",
